# Endpoint Routing Rules

## Main Entry Point

All HTTP requests are handled in [src/index.ts](mdc:src/index.ts) via the `fetch()` handler.

## Request Flow Pattern

```typescript
1. Generate requestId: Date.now().toString(36)
2. Parse URL: new URL(request.url)
3. Log request details with requestId
4. Handle CORS preflight (OPTIONS)
5. Route by pathname
6. Return response with CORS headers
```

## Endpoint Categories

### Core System Endpoints (4)

**Pattern:** Exact pathname match

```typescript
if (url.pathname === '/health') {
  // Health check - used by all dashboards
  // Returns: { status, version, timestamp, requestId, duration }
}

if (url.pathname === '/logs') {
  // Centralized logging - used by browser extension
  // POST: Receives log batches from extension
}

if (url.pathname === '/diagnostics') {
  // System diagnostics - used by setup wizard, health monitor
  // Returns: bindings status, KV status, last checks
}

if (url.pathname === '/system-status') {
  // Detailed status - used by dashboard stats
  // Returns: uptime, memory, KV records, health indicators
}
```

**Used By:** All dashboards, monitoring tools, browser extension

---

### BetTicker Endpoints (3+)

**Pattern:** Exact pathname or prefix match

```typescript
if (url.pathname === '/cloud/api/Manager/getBetTicker') {
  // Transparent proxy + KV interception
  // Handler: handleBetTickerInterception()
  // Location: src/interceptors/bet-ticker-sniffer.ts
  // Returns: Original API response (with side-effect KV storage)
}

if (url.pathname.startsWith('/interceptor/')) {
  // BetTicker history/analysis API
  // Handler: handleInterceptorAPI()
  // Routes:
  //   - /interceptor/history?limit=100
  //   - /interceptor/response?key=...
  //   - /interceptor/stats
}
```

**Used By:** Browser extension, all dashboards

**Documentation:** [docs/BET_TICKER_SNIFFER.md](mdc:docs/BET_TICKER_SNIFFER.md)

---

### MCP Protocol Endpoints (2+)

**Pattern:** Exact pathname or prefix match

```typescript
if (url.pathname === '/mcp') {
  // JSON-RPC 2.0 MCP protocol endpoint
  // Handler: handleMCPRequest()
  // Location: src/mcp/server.ts
  // Methods: initialize, tools/list, tools/call
}

if (url.pathname.startsWith('/tools/')) {
  // Intelligence tools API (13 tools)
  // Handler: handleMCPTools()
  // Routes:
  //   - /tools/getBettingExposure
  //   - /tools/getCLV
  //   - /tools/getSharpScore
  //   - /tools/getHoldPercentage
}
```

**Used By:** Claude Desktop, AI assistants, Dashboard Pro

**Documentation:** [docs/MCP_ENDPOINTS.md](mdc:docs/MCP_ENDPOINTS.md)

